1602	The proof of Theorem~\ref{thm:pauli} is the adaptation, to low individual degree, of the analysis of the quantum low-degree test of Natarajan and Vidick. It is developed in Chapters~\ref{chap:qpbt-observables} and~\ref{chap:qpbt-combining} and concluded in Chapter~\ref{chap:qpbt-extraction}. The formal proof uses proved, directly indexed low-degree inputs and is complete under the standard axioms. The source's seed-indexed derivation still has the divisibility and identification obligations documented in \cite{gap:qpbt_ld-dimension-divisibility}; the blueprint therefore does not place a proof-level formalization mark on that printed proof account. The argument also uses the corrected rigidity statement of Theorem~\ref{thm:ms-rigidity}.
